  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: nimbus-jose-jwt 9.7.0.rhlw-00002",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released com.nimbusds:nimbus-jose-jwt 9.7.0.rhlw-00002 with a backported security fix.\n\nCVE-2023-52428: In Connect2id Nimbus JOSE+JWT before 9.37.2, an attacker can cause a denial of service (resource consumption) via a large JWE p2c header value (aka iteration count) for the PasswordBasedDecrypter (PBKDF2) component.\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for com.nimbusds:nimbus-jose-jwt 9.7.0 from Maven Central.",
